{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Recorded the parent configuration question's account with its second repair path measured. The new receipt 5627b36f50384d14851e4b5da991fa96 shows the node restarting with the snapshot's three-server configuration while the configuration in force already lists a late joiner, then ending with the configuration in force while its snapshot index jumps from 12 to 99 and its last log index stays at its pre-shutdown value — so the restoration arrived with an installed snapshot rather than by log replication. The account now cites four receipts with joint_history (two gap runs, one repair by arriving entry, one repair by installed snapshot), both declared comparisons hold, and the limitation that the snapshot repair was source-derived is replaced by that measurement.\"}"}}
